# Revit Clean Architecture & MVVM Guidelines

## Command Pattern
- Always annotate commands:
  ```csharp
  [Transaction(TransactionMode.Manual)]
  [Regeneration(RegenerationOption.Manual)]
  public class SampleCommand : IExternalCommand
  {
      public Result Execute(ExternalCommandData commandData, ref string message, ElementSet elements)
      {
          try
          {
              // Command logic
              return Result.Succeeded;
          }
          catch (Exception ex)
          {
              message = ex.Message;
              return Result.Failed;
          }
      }
  }
  ```

## MVVM Pattern
- Use `CommunityToolkit.Mvvm` (`ObservableObject`, `[ObservableProperty]`, `[RelayCommand]`).
- The ViewModel must NOT reference Revit API classes directly if possible; keep business logic clean.
- In ViewModels, dispatch Revit API writes through `RevitTask.RunAsync(() => { ... })`.

## Window Ownership
- Modeless windows must set their owner to Revit's main window handle to prevent getting hidden behind Revit:
  ```csharp
  var helper = new System.Windows.Interop.WindowInteropHelper(window);
  helper.Owner = Autodesk.Windows.ComponentManager.ApplicationWindow;
  ```
